ression of Alzheimer disease</article-title><source>Neurology</source><year>2007</year><volume>68</volume><fpage>1083</fpage><lpage>1084</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1212/01.wnl.0000260435.20698.77</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Borroni B, Archetti S, Ferrari M, Cesana BM, Padovani A (2007) Relationship of vascular risk to the progression of Alzheimer disease. Neurology 68:1083&#x02013;1084. doi:10.1212/01.wnl.0000260435.20698.77 author reply 1084 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17389321</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR6"><label>6.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Buccione</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Perri</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Carlesimo</surname><given-names>GA</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Cognitive and behavioural predictors of progression rates in Alzheimer&#x02019;s disease</article-title><source>Eur J Neurol</source><year>2007</year><volume>14</volume><fpage>440</fpage><lpage>446</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1111/j.1468-1331.2007.01693.x</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Buccione I, Perri R, Carlesimo GA et al (2007) Cognitive and behavioural predictors of progression rates in Alzheimer&#x02019;s disease. Eur J Neurol 14:440&#x02013;446. doi:10.1111/j.1468-1331.2007.01693.x <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17388995</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR7"><label>7.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Byrne</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Bucks</surname><given-names>RS</given-names></name><name><surname>Wilcock</surname><given-names>GK</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Mini mental state examination</article-title><source>Lancet</source><year>2000</year><volume>355</volume><fpage>314</fpage><lpage>315</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi"